title: HL-RCS — Sign In with Password
---
sequenceDiagram
autonumber
actor U as User
participant UI as «user interaction» AuthPage / AuthContext
participant C as «control» AuthController
participant S as «service» AuthServiceImpl
participant A as «security» AuthenticationManager / DAO Provider
participant D as «service» CustomUserDetailsService
participant R as «entity» User / Capability Repositories
participant J as «security» JwtTokenProvider
U->>UI: Enter email or phone, password and remember preference
UI->>+C: POST /api/auth/login
Note right of C: Invalid request fields return HTTP 400
C->>+S: login(request)
S->>+A: authenticate(normalized identifier, password)
A->>+D: loadUserByUsername(identifier)
D->>+R: findByEmail; fallback to phone and alternate phone format
R-->>-D: User or not found
opt User found
D->>+R: Find ACTIVE user capabilities
R-->>-D: Capabilities
end
D-->>-A: CustomUserDetails or UsernameNotFoundException
A->>A: Check account state and password hash
A-->>-S: Authentication or authentication exception
alt Invalid credentials
S-->>C: BadCredentialsException
C-->>UI: HTTP 401 — error (via exception handler)
UI-->>U: Show sign-in error
else Account locked or disabled
S-->>C: LockedException / DisabledException
C-->>UI: HTTP 403 — error
UI-->>U: Show account restriction
else Authenticated ACTIVE account
S->>S: Set SecurityContext; verify ACTIVE status
S->>+J: generateToken(authentication)
J-->>-S: JWT access token
S-->>C: AuthResponse with role and capabilities
C-->>UI: HTTP 200 — ApiResponse of AuthResponse
UI->>UI: acceptSession(data, remember); save JWT; set user
UI-->>U: Navigate to authorized destination
end
deactivate S
deactivate C
